Z||000000||William||12-31-1999||01:57 AM||||Gonna paint the fiero next week!!! Looking for comments from those that have had there fiero painted. Did the paint shop paint around the black trim strip or was all the molding removed before it was painted? If so, should I remove it myself or just tell the shop to do it? How about painting the the strip, grills, and bumber pads, should the shop paint them all or did you guys do that part yourselves and save the cash? What gloss level did these black parts have when new? Finally, I'm thinking about painting the mirrors red to match the rest of the car, thoughts?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rick Turner||12-31-1999||03:53 AM||||I just got thru painting my 85 SE, Its a black car. The trim was done on the car using duplicolor bumper paint. The mirrors were done using a black satin finish also Duplicolor. The car was cleaned and sanded. primer was added and car was sanded,reprimed and sanded again until any detected flaws were removed. 1 coat black epoxy primer 1 coat basecoat and 2 coats clear were used. New rubber seals were added to the top and windows. worked out ok for me, looks like new. Good luck on yours.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||12-31-1999||04:46 PM||||Here are some pic's of my friend Bob's 86 GT that he "stole" for $500! The paint job costed him way more than that, but he still doesnt have that much tied up in an 80,000 mile car.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/booth2_1.jpg">  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/paintbooth_1.jpg"> <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/outside.jpg">  <P>The car only had 2 small repairs required, but the previous owner had deciced that he wanted the car to be flat black, so had been spray can painted. Most of the work involved using an orbital sander with 400 grit sandpaper to remove the black. The spoiler, tail lights, marker lights, fuel door and opening, intake grill, rear hood louvers and other small mouldings were removed. The car was then wet sanded with 400 again, sealed with PPG sealer, 2 coats of grey on the lower rockers and trim, 2 coats of red and then 2 coats of PPG high solids urethane clear. I thing Bob will be happy with his "new" car.<p>[This message has been edited by Cooter (edited 12-31-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||12-31-1999||07:03 PM||||I'll say, thats a beautiful paint job! William, I wouldn't let them paint over the trim or grills or anywhere else thats supposed to be black. It'll look tacky! I would leave the mirrors black as well, but that's me. I guess you could always spray can them back if you change your mind after having them painted red.||||reg||14
